ng to recent IUCN estimates, though it fluctuates and might be slightly higher or lower, say ~117,000).\nWait, number of individual giraffes.\nHow many spots per giraffe?\nAn adult giraffe has roughly 100 to 200 spots.\nWait, is it 100-200? Let's check.\nGiraffe coat patterns: Each giraffe has a unique pattern. The number of patches (spots) on a giraffe is typically around 100 to 200.\nLet's refine: A giraffe has about 100-150 spots. But let's look at smaller spots too.\nWait, a quick search in memory: how many spots does a giraffe have? Usually cited around 100-200, some say up to 300.\nLet's take an average of 300 spots per giraffe.\n",
